WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.290
What are you rebelling against?

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.509
What you got.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.219
Canada's freedom convoy started

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.139
three weeks ago with truckers from

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.519
the east and west coasts of that

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.289
country converging on Ottawa to

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.149
protest a law requiring that

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.159
they be vaccinated to come back into

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.078
their own country, given that well

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:17.999
over 80 percent of the truckers are

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.869
vaccinated.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.699
What exactly are they protesting?

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.769
As one reporter who talked to dozens

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.449
of demonstrators put it, it's less

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.099
about vaccine mandates and more

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.139
about a sense that things will never

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.609
go back to normal, a sense that

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.989
they're being ganged up on by the

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.119
government, the media, Big Tech,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.099
Big Pharma truckers complained about

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.049
inflation and about being demonized

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.489
as dumb and irrational.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.499
They feel underappreciated by elites

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.089
who tell them what to do without

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.679
giving them any say in their own

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.929
lives. One protester gave eloquent

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.239
voice to populist resentment, saying

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.499
"There's a group in power that

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.449
always manages to create panic

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.219
among the masses and siphon off

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.259
public funds." The trucker protests

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.079
remind me of the Tea Party in 2009,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.159
Occupy Wall Street in 2011,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.459
the Women's March in 2017

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.229
and Black Lives Matter protests

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.669
after the police killing of Michael

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.679
Brown in 2014 and George

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.969
Floyd in 2020.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.039
Whatever specific event ignited

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.869
each of those movements, they

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.549
all quickly took on greater

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.979
proportions and expressed the vast,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.899
generalized anger not

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.059
simply at overspending, bailouts,

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.159
income inequality, sexism and police

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.349
brutality, but governments

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.209
and cultural elites that seem at

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.949
best indifferent to ordinary

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.139
people's lives and at worst,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.429
downright malevolent.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.529
These movements typify what former

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.389
CIA analyst Martin Guthrie

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.889
wrote about in the Revolt of the

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.109
Public and the Crisis of Authority

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.039
in the New Millennium.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.599
Governments and elites have lost the

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.459
trust and confidence of the people

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.809
they supposedly serve.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.369
Social media and other forms of

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.289
communications empower protest

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.879
movements that are authentic,

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.799
decentralized and leaderless,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.029
at least at the beginning.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.739
They're much better at articulating

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.929
rage and anger at the status quo

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.549
than they are at proposing anything

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.889
like concrete proposals for reform.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.269
That was certainly the case with the

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.069
Tea Party, which started out as a

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.989
revolt against wild spending and

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.638
bank bailouts during the financial

00:02:08.639 --> 00:02:10.079
crisis. The movement brought

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.119
hundreds of thousands of protesters

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.189
to the streets all over the country.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.869
It captured the libertarian

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:18.119
imagination with its simple message

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.799
of controlling government spending

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.389
and holding businesses and people

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.339
accountable for bad decisions

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.079
because capitalism is supposed to be

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.359
a system of profit and loss.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.189
The Tea Party wave got a handful of

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.529
people elected to Congress in 2010

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.479
and 2012, including Senator

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.979
Rand Paul, who's cheering the

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.959
Canadian truckers on an even calling

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.429
for an American version of the

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.449
freedom convoy.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.099
"Clog things up, make people think

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.149
about the mandates.".

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.249
But the Tea Party ultimately faded

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.469
into insignificance and impotence,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.329
in large part because it could only

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.799
articulate frustration and

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.639
negativity.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.229
It was quickly absorbed into a

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.239
Republican party that failed

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.309
at every step to reduce the size,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.839
scope and spending of government.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.699
The Canadian freedom convoy will

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.619
likely suffer a similar fate.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.269
Some of the other recent protest

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.559
movements have been much more

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.419
successful in pushing an agenda,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.339
but all have lost urgency

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.199
and effectiveness as they became

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.269
more centralized and enmeshed

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.799
with Partisan politics.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.779
Their leaders, just like the heads

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.889
of the governments they're

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.749
protesting, abuse their

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.729
power and thus lose their moral

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.439
authority. But that doesn't mean new

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.389
protest movements don't matter.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.229
Far from it.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.789
Even if they don't succeed at

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.409
achieving their stated goals, their

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.419
blows against the status quo whose

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.189
cumulative force will make

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.989
governments and elites become more

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.969
accountable to the very people they

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.229
ultimately rely on.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.879
As with the collapse of communism,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.529
eventually there comes a tipping

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.359
point where the seemingly impossible

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.889
becomes the inevitable.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.629
In a country where arbitrary COVID

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.609
policies still run rampant, trust

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.989
and confidence in government,

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.549
business and organized religion

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.599
continues to fall.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.609
Inflation is at a 40 year high,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.589
and just 17 percent

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.149
of us are satisfied with the way

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:57.959
things are going.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.119
Expect many new movements to rise

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.949
up soon. As a society,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.361
we're like Marlon Brando in "The

00:04:03.362 --> 00:04:05.489
Wild One." We may not know the best

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.809
way forward, exactly.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.849
But that's not going to stop us from

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.319
pushing into the future.

